  "limitations": [
    "The 88-case survey is a feature sample, not a compatibility percentage.",
    "The new rollback route uses component validation and its own checked-image/abstract-journal proofs; it does not reuse the canonical encoder certificate for altered schema text. OS syscall and crash refinement remain a documented trusted boundary.",
    "The retained-catalog rollback route currently applies at the ordinary unreserved 4096-byte geometry and uses the single-page catalog component decoder. Other geometries/conversion and very large schema catalogs need further work.",
    "The new bulk path drops canonical physical caches. Full encoder inversion and optimized state retention for these images, and broad performance measurements, are not established.",
    "SIGKILL timing samples do not cover every syscall boundary or power-loss scenario.",
    "SQL-level sqlite_schema formatting outside the persisted file, all ALTER/index-renaming combinations, extended index kinds and broader SQL/file/WAL semantics remain incomplete."
  ],
